  "pins: {\"network.emit_pb_filter_gate_v2\": true, \"network.phase_leveling\": true, \"network.code_bias_disc_jump_test\": true, \"network.emit_ura\": true, \"network.sbasis_complete\": true, \"network.parallel_max_threads\": 20, \"network.sticky_pivot\": true, \"network.cycle_slip.mw_evidence_refloat\": true, \"network.state_snapshot_carry_lin\": true, \"network.state_snapshot_datum_capture\": true, \"network.state_snapshot_emit_capture\": true, \"network.serialize_disc_counters\": true}",
  "exceptions (deliberately unarmed ledger recommendations): {\"network.clock_datum_sum_to_zero\": \"does NOT graduate (ledger row); the pin datum stays the default\", \"network.resume_frame_restore\": \"sim-validated only (SPEC_synthetic §18.14 leg E, 60-sta sim, 2026-09-06): the warm-resume frame + coupling restore has no FIELD arm yet, and this lineage runs carry_invariant (the coupling restore is out of regime without phase_leveling); arm both on the first field warm-resume validation, writer side first (state_snapshot_frame_capture + _coupling_capture)\", \"network.trace_dd_fractional_ref\": \"CONTINUITY, not doubt: the A/B PASSES the structural half and 'oldest' measurably improves the as-traced grade at a returned-reference hour (SPEC_amb_iono §6.13.3, E h5 0.334 -> 0.195 cyc), but the goldens ARE the comparison baseline and changing which satellite their dd-frac trace references would break continuity with the entire existing record of dd-frac grades.  The golden lineages are graded ref-free (simnet_dd_reref.py / --ref-free), which is strictly better than any reference policy, so they gain nothing and lose comparability.  Arm 'oldest' on a standalone/archival trace, not here.\", \"network.cycle_slip.common_band_scope\": \"FIELD HARNESS EXCEPTION (SPEC_event_harness s20, 2026-09-12): field legs at GOPE00CZE (seed ep0604, 60 epochs, event at +10): single-band slips narrow correctly on real data (E1 L5X -99 -> {L5X}; E2 L1C +37 -> {L1C}; E5 L5X -31 with LLI -> {L5X} via rule F3), but the equal-count L1C+L5X +29 slip on G24 narrowed to the INNOCENT band L2W under BOTH if_phase_td_pairs first and all, because G24 is the IF-TD reference satellite of both L5 chains at that station and a reference arc is UNTESTED in the additional chains (its deviation is ref-minus-ref = 0.000000 by construction; 41 such arcs network-wide = exactly one per station, the highest L5-capable satellite in 80.6 % of epochs, rank <= 2 in 99 %).  At G25 (not the reference) pairs=all vetoes exactly (iftd(L1C+L5X)=flagged, 3.15 m vs 0.109 m) and pairs=first keeps L2W.  On carry_invariant the wrong narrowing has no T4 backstop (attribution 0 for 6 h, RAIM-pool re-host gap) and its wire/consumer cost could not be priced: the field golden cannot warm-resume (61/61 epochs withheld at the seam, SH a00 -4810 TECU; Card 1f carry_coupling_gauge_project is the loader-named prerequisite, fingerprinted, absent from the golden - owed as its own card).  FIX STUB before a field pin: a pair whose IF-TD chain holds the satellite as its reference is NOT silent for the verdict (untested => immature => all-band on that arc), re-priced on G24 and G25; then pin together with if_phase_td_pairs = all on a seed that warm-resumes.  SPEC_event_harness s20.1.\", \"network.cycle_slip.if_phase_td_pairs\": \"FIELD HARNESS EXCEPTION (SPEC_event_harness s20, 2026-09-12): field legs at GOPE00CZE/G25 (equal-count L1C+L5X +29, seed ep0604): all == the (L1C,L5X) IF-TD deviation reads 3.1508 m against a 0.1089 m threshold (29x; 29 cyc x 0.107 m/cyc = 3.10 m predicted) -> veto -> all three bands freed exactly as OFF; first == the pair is never evaluated -> the scope keeps L2W (the innocent band).  The close-spaced pools are healthy on real data (L2W/L5X threshold 0.17 m; the 12x amplification is absorbed; 6 h seed: L1C_L5Q / L1C_L5X pairs 0 flags).  BUT the additional chains do not test their own reference satellite (deviation identically 0 on one arc per station = the highest L5-capable satellite; the first chain's reference arm is not re-run, s14.10.4), so the veto is dead exactly there (G24 at GOPE) - pinned TOGETHER with common_band_scope once the reference-arc clause lands and the field seed can warm-resume (Card 1f).  SPEC_event_harness s20.1.\", \"network.scoped_handover_response\": \"GPS-ONLY lineage: the knob's entire benefit is sparing the OTHER constellation's carry at a pivot handover, so with one constellation there is nothing to spare and it is structurally inert (the regime predicate already excludes it; this entry is the record, not a suppression).  Arm it when the field lineage becomes multi-constellation — a field arm is owed then.\", \"network.handover_stransform\": \"PREREQUISITE IS ITSELF A FIELD EXCEPTION: network.handover_stransform requires network.scoped_handover_response, which is excepted on this GPS-only lineage, so the regime predicate is false here and the knob is out of regime rather than suppressed.  This entry is the record.  Sim-validated on two beds (SPEC_event_harness §19.6); a FIELD ARM IS OWED, and it is owed behind the prerequisite's field arm, not independently of it.\"}",
